    "updated_at": "2021-07-12T21:51:29Z",
    "body": "> one is never sure which ID to link to,\r\n\r\nI think the example you gave is actually reasonable - it would be *okay* for both to link to the dfn, but the way the second case is written, a section link is also perfectly appropriate, and would be fine to stay as it is even if the dfn was moved into an intro paragraph for the section.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nI agree that having headings be the link targets for some definitions makes a lot of sense for many things. I've also gotten a feature request to let this occur even for dfns that *aren't* in the heading - letting someone put an attribute on a dfn that makes it use the nearest heading's ID as the linking destination for that attribute, instead.\r\n\r\nSo perhaps this should move to WebRef, with the current markup pattern being implicitly recognized as triggering this behavior as well.",
